\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Three-dimensional rotational dynamics of Magic Gems. (a)~Universal principal inertia ratio $I_\perp (\lambda )/I_{zz}=\frac  12(1+\lambda ^2(n^2+1))$ versus vertical scale $\lambda $ for orders $n=3,4,5$, with 3D inertia ellipsoids at the cubic 3D-print scale $\lambda _{\mathrm  {cube}}=1/5$ ($21/25$), the isotropic spherical-top transition $\lambda _{\mathrm  {iso}}=1/\sqrt  {17}$ ($1$), and the canonical lift $\lambda =1$ ($9$) for $n=4$. (b)~Triaxial Poinsot energy ellipsoid $\frac  12\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ I_k\omega _k^2=E$ of entry-weighted square \#46 ($I_1=110<I_2=230<I_3=340$), showing the figure-eight separatrix through the unstable intermediate saddle $\pm \boldsymbol  \omega _2$ and the heteroclinic polhode orbit connecting $+\omega _2$ to $-\omega _2$. (c)~Time series of Euler's equations \eqref  {eq:euler}: an axisymmetric magic rotor (D\"urer \#175 or any point-weighted gem) precesses harmonically with constant $|\boldsymbol  \omega _\perp |$, whereas entry-weighted square \#46 ($|Q_{xy}|=60$) undergoes periodic $180^\circ $ Dzhanibekov flips $\omega _2(t)\in [+1,-1]$ about its intermediate diagonal axis. (d)~Census of the quadrupole moment $|Q_{xy}(S)|=|\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ z_{ij}x_jy_i|=\frac  12(I_2-I_1)$ across the $880$ order-four magic squares.}}{12}{figure.66}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:precession}{{4}{12}{Three-dimensional rotational dynamics of Magic Gems. (a)~Universal principal inertia ratio $I_\perp (\lambda )/I_{zz}=\frac 12(1+\lambda ^2(n^2+1))$ versus vertical scale $\lambda $ for orders $n=3,4,5$, with 3D inertia ellipsoids at the cubic 3D-print scale $\lambda _{\mathrm {cube}}=1/5$ ($21/25$), the isotropic spherical-top transition $\lambda _{\mathrm {iso}}=1/\sqrt {17}$ ($1$), and the canonical lift $\lambda =1$ ($9$) for $n=4$. (b)~Triaxial Poinsot energy ellipsoid $\frac 12\sum I_k\omega _k^2=E$ of entry-weighted square \#46 ($I_1=110<I_2=230<I_3=340$), showing the figure-eight separatrix through the unstable intermediate saddle $\pm \boldsymbol \omega _2$ and the heteroclinic polhode orbit connecting $+\omega _2$ to $-\omega _2$. (c)~Time series of Euler's equations \eqref {eq:euler}: an axisymmetric magic rotor (D\"urer \#175 or any point-weighted gem) precesses harmonically with constant $|\boldsymbol \omega _\perp |$, whereas entry-weighted square \#46 ($|Q_{xy}|=60$) undergoes periodic $180^\circ $ Dzhanibekov flips $\omega _2(t)\in [+1,-1]$ about its intermediate diagonal axis. (d)~Census of the quadrupole moment $|Q_{xy}(S)|=|\sum z_{ij}x_jy_i|=\frac 12(I_2-I_1)$ across the $880$ order-four magic squares}{figure.66}{}}
