\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Wireframes, complete $K_{16}$ strut networks, and unfolded papercraft cutout nets of Magic Gems \cite  {mathewson2025magicgemweb}. (a)~Nested ball-and-rod wireframe $G(\mathcal  G_0)\cup G(\mathcal  G_1)$ of Gem \#673 ($17$ outer blue rods + $17$ inner orange rods), where tuning the inner-to-outer rod diameter ratio to $d_1/d_0=0.793$ at $\lambda =1$ ($0.493$ at $\lambda =0.20$) restores $\mathbf  c_{\mathrm  {wire}}=\mathbf  0$. (b)~Fully interconnected complete network $K_{16}$ of D\"urer's Gem \#175 (\texttt  {magicGem\_v2.stl}) with all $\binom  {16}{2}=120$ rods ($24$ outer hull edges in green + $96$ internal cross-struts in slate) and $16$ node cubes; for equal-mass rods, $\mathbf  c(K_{16})=\mathbf  0$ and $\Sigma _{\mathrm  {rods}}=\frac  {29}{45}\Sigma (\lambda )$ for all $880$ squares (\Cref  {thm:complete-network}(1)). (c)~Exact 2D unfolded papercraft cutout net of D\"urer's Gem \#175 ($\lambda =0.20$, $f=(12,24,14)$) rooted at $\bigstar F_0$, with $f_2-1=13$ dashed fold lines (mean dihedral fold angle $\overline  {\theta }_{\mathrm  {fold}}=141.2^\circ \in [117^\circ ,165^\circ ]$), $2f_0-2=22$ solid cut perimeter segments, $N_{\mathrm  {tabs}}=f_0-1=11$ grey trapezoidal glue tabs paired with their mating cut edges by lowercase labels \texttt  {a}--\texttt  {k} (\Cref  {prop:papercraft-net}(1)), and magic entries $s_{ij}$ at the unfolded vertices. (d)~Comparison of mean centroid drift $\|\mathbf  c(S)\|_2$ across all $880$ order-four magic squares for the five physical realizations at $\lambda =1.0$ and $\lambda =0.20$.}}{19}{figure.115}\protected@file@percent }
